  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Organisations pay for better hiring, clearer performance conversations and fewer people surprises. They judge you by trust, evidence and the usefulness of your advice.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is understanding how the business earns before advising on how its people should be organised.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and HR business partner: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft policies, screen applications and summarise survey comments. Routine HR administration shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, confidentiality and trust hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and check; later, own advice and sensitive conversations.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general HR business partner path</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
